# The Back Door in an Apparently Chaotic Map

The Collatz rule is easy to run and notoriously difficult to understand globally. This presentation asks a narrower cryptographic question: does iteration make the rule hard to reverse? Explore the map itself at the [Collatz conjecture overview](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collatz_conjecture), then construct the exact answer below.

